ntdll: a process's memory counters on macOS from the task's physical footprint, not its virtual size.

fill_vm_counters reported the Mach task's virtual size as PagefileUsage (and resident plus virtual as
VirtualSize), which kernelbase hands out as PrivateUsage too. The virtual size counts every reservation of the
host process, and the x86-64 emulator reserves its guest address space and lookup tables in the hundreds of GB:
a 17 MB probe under the arm64 engine reported 463,651 MB of page file usage with a 17 MB working set. A program
that budgets on that figure starves itself: Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024's own session trace recorded
639,388,984 KiB "in use" on a 32 GB Mac, kept 102 MB of textures on the GPU and scaled its terrain level of
detail to a quarter (terrainLodMilli 251), which is the coarse Free Flight map and menu globe that no graphics
setting changed. Windows reports the private commit; the task's physical footprint (TASK_VM_INFO) is the
closest figure macOS keeps, so PagefileUsage, PeakPagefileUsage and VirtualSize come from it now (the probe:
16 MB, 16 MB, 34 MB). Found on the M4 on 2026-10-16 (private/notes/msfs-2024-arm64-boot-2026-10-15.md).
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index 9dad6c3..b1cfc44 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -999,8 +999,18 @@ void fill_vm_counters( VM_COUNTERS_EX *pvmi, int unix_pid )
     infoCount = MACH_TASK_BASIC_INFO_COUNT;
     if(task_info(mach_task_self(), MACH_TASK_BASIC_INFO, (task_info_t)&info, &infoCount) == KERN_SUCCESS)
     {
-        pvmi->VirtualSize = info.resident_size + info.virtual_size;
-        pvmi->PagefileUsage = info.virtual_size;
+        /* The Mach virtual size counts every reservation of the host process, which an emulator of another
+         * architecture makes in the hundreds of GB; a program that budgets on PagefileUsage then starves itself.
+         * Windows reports the private commit, which the task's physical footprint approximates best. */
+        task_vm_info_data_t vm_info;
+        mach_msg_type_number_t vmCount = TASK_VM_INFO_COUNT;
+        ULONG64 footprint = info.resident_size;
+        if (task_info(mach_task_self(), TASK_VM_INFO, (task_info_t)&vm_info, &vmCount) == KERN_SUCCESS && vm_info.phys_footprint)
+            footprint = vm_info.phys_footprint;
+        pvmi->VirtualSize = footprint + info.resident_size;
+        pvmi->PeakVirtualSize = pvmi->VirtualSize;
+        pvmi->PagefileUsage = footprint;
+        pvmi->PeakPagefileUsage = footprint;
         pvmi->WorkingSetSize = info.resident_size;
         pvmi->PeakWorkingSetSize = info.resident_size_max;
     }
